PUBLIC RESPONSE: {C}

The ESA requires employers with 25+ employees (counted on Jan 1 of the year) to maintain written policies on both disconnecting from work and electronic monitoring. Any revised policy must be distributed to every current employee within 30 days of the revision (and to new hires within 30 days of hire).  

Option C is the only employer that meets the 25-employee threshold on the relevant date and is therefore obligated to comply. Its practice of revising the policies monthly but distributing the updates only quarterly necessarily means some revisions reach employees after the 30-day statutory window, violating the distribution rule. All other options are below the 25-employee threshold on the dates that trigger the obligations, so they are not required to have (or distribute) either policy.

